# Generated output whose generator does NOT go through prettier. A
# formatter and a generator cannot both be the author of the same bytes:
# prettier reflows a short JSON array onto one line, `JSON.stringify(x,
# null, 2)` does not, and whichever ran last wins. The result is a format
# gate that goes red on a commit which only regenerated an artefact, and
# that is how a gate gets switched off.
#
# Nothing is lost. Each of these has a --check gate of its own, which is
# the stricter test: it compares the artefact against the code it
# describes, not against a style.
#
#   landing/demo          npm run demo:build
#   public-facts.json     npm run facts
#   monitor-type-dod.json npm run dod
#   kuma-mapping.json     npm run kuma:matrix
#
# docs/MIGRATION.md and docs/MONITOR-TYPE-DOD.md are deliberately NOT
# here. Their generators format the page through this repository's own
# prettier before writing it, so the two already agree - and listing them
# breaks the generator rather than protecting it, because the prettier
# CLI honours this file: `migration:check` started failing the moment
# they were added, comparing an unformatted render against a formatted
# page. docs/HIGH-FREQUENCY.md is not here either; bench:check only reads
# it, so it is hand-written prose.
#
# Patterns are gitignore syntax, so a trailing comment on a pattern line
# becomes part of the pattern and silently matches nothing. That is why
# the generator names are listed above rather than beside each path.
landing/demo
public-facts.json
monitor-type-dod.json
kuma-mapping.json
